vkQuake: keep the colour buffer at RGBA8 on Broadcom V3D.

NEW for vkquake-drm (docs/gpu-new-lane/vkquake-perf.md section 3). vkQuake picks
A2B10G10R10_UNORM_PACK32 for its scene colour buffer whenever the device can render and
sample it. V3D 4.x stores RGB10_A2 in the tile buffer at 16F (v3dvx_formats.c,
V3D_INTERNAL_TYPE_16F), i.e. 64 bpp, which drops the tile size one step (64x64 -> 64x32)
for the main pass and the GUI subpass, doubling their tile count. In memory both formats
are 4 B/px, so the 10-bit buffer buys nothing but that cost here. The check is on the PCI
vendor ID v3dv reports (0x14E4, Broadcom), not on the OS; the old lane rendered RGBA8.

--- a/Quake/gl_vidsdl.c
+++ b/Quake/gl_vidsdl.c
@@ -1427,7 +1427,12 @@
 	// Find color buffer format
 	vulkan_globals.color_format = VK_FORMAT_R8G8B8A8_UNORM;
 
-	if (extended_format_support == VK_TRUE)
+	// Broadcom V3D 4.x keeps RGB10_A2 in the tile buffer at 16F (64 bpp), twice RGBA8's size, which
+	// halves the tile size of every pass that renders to the colour buffer. The memory footprint is
+	// the same 4 B/px, so the 10-bit buffer only costs there: stay on RGBA8.
+	if (vulkan_globals.device_properties.vendorID == 0x14E4)
+		Con_Printf ("Using R8G8B8A8 color buffer format (V3D: RGB10_A2 is 16F in the tile buffer)\n");
+	else if (extended_format_support == VK_TRUE)
 	{
 		vkGetPhysicalDeviceFormatProperties (vulkan_physical_device, VK_FORMAT_A2B10G10R10_UNORM_PACK32, &format_properties);
 		qboolean a2_b10_g10_r10_support = (format_properties.optimalTilingFeatures & REQUIRED_COLOR_BUFFER_FEATURES) == REQUIRED_COLOR_BUFFER_FEATURES;
